15 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows healthy green rice leaves with small droplets of water. Panel B displays a rice leaf with two elongated gray lesions surrounded by brown borders. Panel C depicts multiple rice leaves with extensive brown lesions and discoloration. Panel D presents a rice leaf with a long, white, necrotic streak along its length. Panel E illustrates a rice leaf with multiple small brown spots scattered on its surface. Panel F shows a rice leaf exhibiting a broad brown streak with a yellowish border.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 34 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Twelve-panel figure showing close-up photos of a green leaf with a brown and yellow lesion, labeled A to L. Each panel shows the same lesion with slight variations in lighting, focus, or color balance. Panel L appears to have a brightly colored magenta and black background, contrasting with the natural backgrounds in other panels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Diagram showing two neural network architectures labeled A and B. Both start with an input node, proceed through a series of colored blocks representing layers like channel splitting, group convolution, depthwise convolution, and max pooling, and use concatenation and channel shuffle before output. Diagram A includes sequential group convolution, depthwise convolution, and concatenation, while diagram B splits after input into max pooling and group convolution paths that merge before channel shuffle. Both use batch normalization and activation functions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 52 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a smartphone home screen with several colorful app icons and a highlighted \215classification\216 button. Panel B displays an illustration of a cartoon farmer with a magnifying glass and clipboard inspecting rice plants, with \215Photo-based Identification\216 and \215Album Selection\216 buttons below. Panel C features the same illustrated farmer, magnifying glass and clipboard visible, with a green banner labeled \215Plant Leaf Disease Identification.\216 Panel D presents a close-up photograph of a rice leaf exhibiting white streaks, matched with the prediction \215Rice Bacterial Leaf Blight\216 and a confidence score of ninety-seven percent at the top, alongside the identification buttons.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 53 0 R /Alt (Panel A displays a line chart titled \215Validation Loss Curves\216 showing ten deep learning models with validation loss rapidly decreasing over two hundred epochs and stabilizing near zero. Panel B shows a line chart titled \215Validation Accuracy Curves\216 comparing the same ten models, with accuracy increasing sharply in early epochs and plateauing above ninety percent. Both panels include distinct colored lines for each model, with legends identifying all models.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 54 0 R /Alt (Ten confusion matrix heatmaps comparing classification results across different models, each labeled A to J. Darker blue shades indicate higher values, with true labels on the y-axis and predicted labels on the x-axis for six classes. Each subplot includes a model name, such as MobileNetv1, ShuffleNetv1, or LMRNet, and a color scale bar to the right of each matrix.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Table with six rows showing rice leaf conditions\204healthy, rice blast, sheath blight, bacterial blight of rice, rice brown spot, and bacterial leaf streak\204with four columns for original image, stage one, stage three, and stage five heatmap visualizations mapping progression of visible disease features.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 44 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt (Grid of rice leaf images in six rows labeled healthy, rice blast, sheath blight, bacterial blight of rice, rice brown spot, and bacterial leaf streak, and four columns labeled original image, stage 1, stage 3, and stage 5. Each stage image uses a thermal-like color mapping to highlight affected areas, showing increased color intensity from left to right.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 45 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
